HST Office: the ribbon's layout dump shows the width the ladder counted for each group.

With HST_RIBBON_DUMP_LAYOUT a group's entry gets "ladder_w": the width Width() last gave the tab's ladder, next
to the rect the group got. A group wider than the ladder counted pushes the tab past its track (Sheets › Chèn on
Linux at 1920: 45 px past the banner's margin); the dump shows which.

- vcl/source/control/HstRibbonV3Layout.cxx (Group::ladderWidth, Width(), Dump()).

License: these upstream-derived files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-ribbon-v3-dumps.py reads it (information).

